window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b344-0caffcd469c9814a.json"]={sha256:"0caffcd469c9814a1ff5dc3bc3ea70dae99741182441f5b53b7da755c72eef6d",value:{"id":"b344","title":"道碴清篩與再利用","titleEn":"Ballast cleaning and reuse","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"道碴清篩與再利用以「粒徑分離再利用物料帳與排水性能」為主線，將十個物理或系統問題拆成機制、計算、驗證與診斷。清篩將受污染道碴分成可再用粗料與廢細料，回收比例不能取代粒形、強度及排水驗證；含水率和顆粒損傷會影響質量帳的解讀。每個單元附帶可重算的假想數據與敏感度，學員需提交帶單位的工作表、可區分失效的證據及模型邊界。","summaryEn":"This course develops gradation separation reuse mass accounts and drainage performance through ten physical or systems questions, each studied through mechanism, calculation, verification and diagnosis. Cleaning separates fouled ballast into reusable coarse material and discarded fines, but recovery fraction cannot replace checks on particle shape, strength and drainage; moisture and particle damage affect the mass account. Every unit contains reproducible assumed inputs and a sensitivity calculation. Learners submit a worksheet with units, discriminating evidence for failures, and explicit model boundaries.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-track","subcategoryTitle":"軌道與土建工程","subcategoryTitleEn":"Track and civil engineering","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-track","learningTags":["rail","rail-track","track"],"architectureFamily":"rail-track","architectureNodes":[["道碴挖取","Ballast excavation"],["粒徑清篩","Particle screening"],["補碴輸送","Ballast supply"],["排水孔隙","Drainage voids"],["復舊幾何","Restored geometry"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-track","labels":["道碴挖取","粒徑清篩","補碴輸送","排水孔隙","復舊幾何"],"labelsEn":["Ballast excavation","Particle screening","Ballast supply","Drainage voids","Restored geometry"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為跨單元的原創假想工作表。先用第一單元定義邊界與單位，再以第二單元檢查另一個控制量，最後用第三單元提出前兩式未涵蓋的另一個檢查問題。原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：feed=100 t, coarse=72 t, fines=25 t；y=feed-coarse-fines=3 t。只把 feed 增加百分之十，y=13 t。模型邊界：各料流均為同時間窗乾質量；差額包含存量變化；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：reusable=72 t, feed=100 t；y=reusable/feed*100=72 percent。只把 reusable 增加百分之十，y=79.2 percent。模型邊界：可再用質量已通過另列的材料檢查；比例不是檢驗合格概率；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。把兩個算例的單一輸入敏感度放在同一張決策表，說明哪個變化最值得先量測；不可把不同物理量的裸數字直接比較，也不可把任一結果當成實際設備的設計、施工或營運許可。","textEn":"This original worksheet connects the first three units using assumed inputs. Establish boundaries and units with the first unit, examine another controlling quantity with the second, and use the third to pose a separate check outside the first two equations. Original assumed example, not field operating values: feed=100 t, coarse=72 t, fines=25 t; y=feed-coarse-fines=3 t. Increasing only feed with a ten-percent increase gives y=13 t. Boundary: All streams use dry mass over the same time window; the residual includes inventory change; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Original assumed example, not field operating values: reusable=72 t, feed=100 t; y=reusable/feed*100=72 percent. Increasing only reusable with a ten-percent increase gives y=79.2 percent. Boundary: Reusable mass has passed separate property checks; the ratio is not a probability of acceptance; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.Put both single-input sensitivities in one decision table and explain which change most deserves measurement. Do not compare bare numbers with different physical dimensions, and do not treat any result as design approval, a construction procedure or operating permission.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b344-v16-s1","title":"清篩質量守恆與可再用材料比例","titleEn":"Cleaning mass conservation & Reusable material fraction","description":"本階段聚焦「清篩質量守恆」與「可再用材料比例」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cleaning mass conservation\" and \"Reusable material fraction\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b344-v16-01","title":"清篩質量守恆：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cleaning mass conservation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「清篩質量守恆」如何影響道碴清篩與再利用的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cleaning mass conservation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ballast cleaning and reuse”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"輸入減已知輸出應對應存量變化與量測差。本模型把 feed 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 13 t。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。各料流均為同時間窗乾質量；差額包含存量變化。使用各料流同步乾質量作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；未記錄存料會把正常暫存當成損耗，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「清篩質量守恆」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Input minus known outputs corresponds to inventory change and measurement discrepancy. In this model, feed is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 13 t. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. All streams use dry mass over the same time window; the residual includes inventory change. Use synchronized dry mass in each material stream as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Unrecorded inventory makes temporary storage appear as loss; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cleaning mass conservation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：feed=100 t, coarse=72 t, fines=25 t；y=feed-coarse-fines=3 t。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: feed=100 t, coarse=72 t, fines=25 t; y=feed-coarse-fines=3 t.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未記錄存料會把正常暫存當成損耗」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Unrecorded inventory makes temporary storage appear as loss.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「清篩質量守恆」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cleaning mass conservation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-01-k1","title":"清篩質量守恆","titleEn":"Cleaning mass conservation","text":"輸入減已知輸出應對應存量變化與量測差。本模型把 feed 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 13 t。","textEn":"Input minus known outputs corresponds to inventory change and measurement discrepancy. In this model, feed is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未記錄存料會把正常暫存當成損耗 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Unrecorded inventory makes temporary storage appear as loss. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「清篩質量守恆」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cleaning mass conservation\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未記錄存料會把正常暫存當成損耗","輸入減已知輸出應對應存量變化與量測差。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：高回收率也可能保留脆弱顆粒"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Unrecorded inventory makes temporary storage appear as loss.","Input minus known outputs corresponds to inventory change and measurement discrepancy.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A high recovery fraction may retain weak particles."],"answer":1,"explanation":"輸入減已知輸出應對應存量變化與量測差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Input minus known outputs corresponds to inventory change and measurement discrepancy. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b344-v16-02","title":"清篩質量守恆：定量估算","titleEn":"Cleaning mass conservation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「清篩質量守恆」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cleaning mass conservation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：feed=100 t, coarse=72 t, fines=25 t；y=feed-coarse-fines=3 t。只把 feed 增加百分之十，y=13 t。模型邊界：各料流均為同時間窗乾質量；差額包含存量變化；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: feed=100 t, coarse=72 t, fines=25 t; y=feed-coarse-fines=3 t. Increasing only feed with a ten-percent increase gives y=13 t. Boundary: All streams use dry mass over the same time window; the residual includes inventory change; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以各料流同步乾質量區分模型與觀察，先用同步料流秤重、含水率修正及設備內存料盤點建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use synchronized dry mass in each material stream to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：feed=100 t, coarse=72 t, fines=25 t；y=feed-coarse-fines=3 t。只把 feed 增加百分之十，y=13 t。模型邊界：各料流均為同時間窗乾質量；差額包含存量變化；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: feed=100 t, coarse=72 t, fines=25 t; y=feed-coarse-fines=3 t. Increasing only feed with a ten-percent increase gives y=13 t. Boundary: All streams use dry mass over the same time window; the residual includes inventory change; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「清篩質量守恆」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cleaning mass conservation\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：混用濕基與乾基含水率會破壞物料平衡","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用岩石密度會低估運輸與暫存體積","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：feed=100 t, coarse=72 t, fines=25 t；y=feed-coarse-fines=3 t。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing wet-basis and dry-basis moisture corrupts mass balance.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Solid-rock density understates transport and storage volume.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: feed=100 t, coarse=72 t, fines=25 t; y=feed-coarse-fines=3 t."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：feed=100 t, coarse=72 t, fines=25 t；y=feed-coarse-fines=3 t。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: feed=100 t, coarse=72 t, fines=25 t; y=feed-coarse-fines=3 t. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b344-v16-03","title":"清篩質量守恆：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cleaning mass conservation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「清篩質量守恆」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cleaning mass conservation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以各料流同步乾質量區分模型與觀察，先用同步料流秤重、含水率修正及設備內存料盤點建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「清篩質量守恆」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use synchronized dry mass in each material stream to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synchronized stream weighing, moisture correction and machine inventory reconciliation, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Cleaning mass conservation. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「清篩質量守恆」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出各料流均為同時間窗乾質量；差額包含存量變化如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由未記錄存料會把正常暫存當成損耗造成偏離的合成觀察，以各料流同步乾質量說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Cleaning mass conservation, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: All streams use dry mass over the same time window; the residual includes inventory change. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Unrecorded inventory makes temporary storage appear as loss. Explain which evidence in synchronized dry mass in each material stream distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：未記錄存料會把正常暫存當成損耗。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Unrecorded inventory makes temporary storage appear as loss. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以各料流同步乾質量區分模型與觀察，先用同步料流秤重、含水率修正及設備內存料盤點建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「清篩質量守恆」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use synchronized dry mass in each material stream to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synchronized stream weighing, moisture correction and machine inventory reconciliation, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Cleaning mass conservation. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「清篩質量守恆」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出各料流均為同時間窗乾質量；差額包含存量變化如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由未記錄存料會把正常暫存當成損耗造成偏離的合成觀察，以各料流同步乾質量說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Cleaning mass conservation, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: All streams use dry mass over the same time window; the residual includes inventory change. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Unrecorded inventory makes temporary storage appear as loss. Explain which evidence in synchronized dry mass in each material stream distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「清篩質量守恆」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cleaning mass conservation\"?","options":["本單元以各料流同步乾質量區分模型與觀察，先用同步料流秤重、含水率修正及設備內存料盤點建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：不同取樣位置會被誤認為破碎增量"],"optionsEn":["Use synchronized dry mass in each material stream to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Different sampling positions can imitate breakage growth."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以各料流同步乾質量區分模型與觀察，先用同步料流秤重、含水率修正及設備內存料盤點建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use synchronized dry mass in each material stream to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b344-v16-04","title":"清篩質量守恆：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cleaning mass conservation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「清篩質量守恆」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cleaning mass conservation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"未記錄存料會把正常暫存當成損耗。這個失效與「清篩質量守恆」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查各料流同步乾質量，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Unrecorded inventory makes temporary storage appear as loss. This failure and a measurement bias in Cleaning mass conservation can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check synchronized dry mass in each material stream rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用各料流同步乾質量作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；未記錄存料會把正常暫存當成損耗，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Unrecorded inventory makes temporary storage appear as loss; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未記錄存料會把正常暫存當成損耗」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Unrecorded inventory makes temporary storage appear as loss.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"未記錄存料會把正常暫存當成損耗。這個失效與「清篩質量守恆」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查各料流同步乾質量，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Unrecorded inventory makes temporary storage appear as loss. This failure and a measurement bias in Cleaning mass conservation can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check synchronized dry mass in each material stream rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「清篩質量守恆」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cleaning mass conservation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","未記錄存料會把正常暫存當成損耗。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：高回收率也可能保留脆弱顆粒"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Unrecorded inventory makes temporary storage appear as loss.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A high recovery fraction may retain weak particles."],"answer":1,"explanation":"未記錄存料會把正常暫存當成損耗。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unrecorded inventory makes temporary storage appear as loss. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b344-v16-05","title":"可再用材料比例：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Reusable material fraction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「可再用材料比例」如何影響道碴清篩與再利用的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Reusable material fraction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ballast cleaning and reuse”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"回收率是物料比例而非材料性能合格率。本模型把 reusable 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 79.2 percent。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。可再用質量已通過另列的材料檢查；比例不是檢驗合格概率。使用粗料質量與獨立性能試驗作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；高回收率也可能保留脆弱顆粒，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「可再用材料比例」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Recovery is a material fraction rather than a performance acceptance rate. In this model, reusable is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 79.2 percent. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Reusable mass has passed separate property checks; the ratio is not a probability of acceptance. Use coarse mass and independent property tests as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. A high recovery fraction may retain weak particles; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Reusable material fraction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：reusable=72 t, feed=100 t；y=reusable/feed*100=72 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: reusable=72 t, feed=100 t; y=reusable/feed*100=72 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：高回收率也可能保留脆弱顆粒」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A high recovery fraction may retain weak particles.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「可再用材料比例」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Reusable material fraction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-05-k1","title":"可再用材料比例","titleEn":"Reusable material fraction","text":"回收率是物料比例而非材料性能合格率。本模型把 reusable 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 79.2 percent。","textEn":"Recovery is a material fraction rather than a performance acceptance rate. In this model, reusable is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：高回收率也可能保留脆弱顆粒 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A high recovery fraction may retain weak particles. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「可再用材料比例」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Reusable material fraction\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：高回收率也可能保留脆弱顆粒","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把全部粗料視為合格會低估新料","回收率是物料比例而非材料性能合格率。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A high recovery fraction may retain weak particles.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating all coarse material as qualified understates fresh demand.","Recovery is a material fraction rather than a performance acceptance rate."],"answer":2,"explanation":"回收率是物料比例而非材料性能合格率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Recovery is a material fraction rather than a performance acceptance rate. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b344-v16-06","title":"可再用材料比例：定量估算","titleEn":"Reusable material fraction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「可再用材料比例」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Reusable material fraction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：reusable=72 t, feed=100 t；y=reusable/feed*100=72 percent。只把 reusable 增加百分之十，y=79.2 percent。模型邊界：可再用質量已通過另列的材料檢查；比例不是檢驗合格概率；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: reusable=72 t, feed=100 t; y=reusable/feed*100=72 percent. Increasing only reusable with a ten-percent increase gives y=79.2 percent. Boundary: Reusable mass has passed separate property checks; the ratio is not a probability of acceptance; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以粗料質量與獨立性能試驗區分模型與觀察，先用乾質量秤重、粒形與強度試驗的批次對照建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use coarse mass and independent property tests to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：reusable=72 t, feed=100 t；y=reusable/feed*100=72 percent。只把 reusable 增加百分之十，y=79.2 percent。模型邊界：可再用質量已通過另列的材料檢查；比例不是檢驗合格概率；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: reusable=72 t, feed=100 t; y=reusable/feed*100=72 percent. Increasing only reusable with a ten-percent increase gives y=79.2 percent. Boundary: Reusable mass has passed separate property checks; the ratio is not a probability of acceptance; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「可再用材料比例」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Reusable material fraction\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：reusable=72 t, feed=100 t；y=reusable/feed*100=72 percent。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：篩網堵塞會讓細料被錯列為粗料","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：短時峰值不代表整班處理量"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: reusable=72 t, feed=100 t; y=reusable/feed*100=72 percent.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Screen clogging misclassifies fines as coarse material.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A short peak rate does not represent shift production."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：reusable=72 t, feed=100 t；y=reusable/feed*100=72 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: reusable=72 t, feed=100 t; y=reusable/feed*100=72 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b344-v16-07","title":"可再用材料比例：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Reusable material fraction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「可再用材料比例」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Reusable material fraction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以粗料質量與獨立性能試驗區分模型與觀察，先用乾質量秤重、粒形與強度試驗的批次對照建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「可再用材料比例」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use coarse mass and independent property tests to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using dry-mass weighing and batch-matched particle-shape and strength tests, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Reusable material fraction. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「可再用材料比例」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出可再用質量已通過另列的材料檢查；比例不是檢驗合格概率如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由高回收率也可能保留脆弱顆粒造成偏離的合成觀察，以粗料質量與獨立性能試驗說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Reusable material fraction, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Reusable mass has passed separate property checks; the ratio is not a probability of acceptance. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A high recovery fraction may retain weak particles. Explain which evidence in coarse mass and independent property tests distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：高回收率也可能保留脆弱顆粒。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A high recovery fraction may retain weak particles. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以粗料質量與獨立性能試驗區分模型與觀察，先用乾質量秤重、粒形與強度試驗的批次對照建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「可再用材料比例」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use coarse mass and independent property tests to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using dry-mass weighing and batch-matched particle-shape and strength tests, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Reusable material fraction. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「可再用材料比例」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出可再用質量已通過另列的材料檢查；比例不是檢驗合格概率如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由高回收率也可能保留脆弱顆粒造成偏離的合成觀察，以粗料質量與獨立性能試驗說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Reusable material fraction, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Reusable mass has passed separate property checks; the ratio is not a probability of acceptance. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A high recovery fraction may retain weak particles. Explain which evidence in coarse mass and independent property tests distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「可再用材料比例」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Reusable material fraction\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以粗料質量與獨立性能試驗區分模型與觀察，先用乾質量秤重、粒形與強度試驗的批次對照建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：空氣滯留會使初期流量不能代表穩態"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use coarse mass and independent property tests to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Trapped air makes initial flow unrepresentative of steady flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以粗料質量與獨立性能試驗區分模型與觀察，先用乾質量秤重、粒形與強度試驗的批次對照建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use coarse mass and independent property tests to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b344-v16-08","title":"可再用材料比例：失效診斷","titleEn":"Reusable material fraction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「可再用材料比例」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Reusable material fraction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"高回收率也可能保留脆弱顆粒。這個失效與「可再用材料比例」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查粗料質量與獨立性能試驗，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A high recovery fraction may retain weak particles. This failure and a measurement bias in Reusable material fraction can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check coarse mass and independent property tests rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用粗料質量與獨立性能試驗作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；高回收率也可能保留脆弱顆粒，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A high recovery fraction may retain weak particles; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：高回收率也可能保留脆弱顆粒」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A high recovery fraction may retain weak particles.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"高回收率也可能保留脆弱顆粒。這個失效與「可再用材料比例」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查粗料質量與獨立性能試驗，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"A high recovery fraction may retain weak particles. This failure and a measurement bias in Reusable material fraction can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check coarse mass and independent property tests rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「可再用材料比例」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Reusable material fraction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把全部粗料視為合格會低估新料","高回收率也可能保留脆弱顆粒。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating all coarse material as qualified understates fresh demand.","A high recovery fraction may retain weak particles."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高回收率也可能保留脆弱顆粒。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A high recovery fraction may retain weak particles. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b344-v16-s2","title":"補充新道碴需求與含水率乾重換算","titleEn":"Fresh ballast requirement & Moisture dry-mass conversion","description":"本階段聚焦「補充新道碴需求」與「含水率乾重換算」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Fresh ballast requirement\" and \"Moisture dry-mass conversion\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b344-v16-09","title":"補充新道碴需求：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Fresh ballast requirement: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「補充新道碴需求」如何影響道碴清篩與再利用的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fresh ballast requirement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ballast cleaning and reuse”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"需求扣除合格回料才得到新料需求。本模型把 demand 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 32.5 t。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。需求不少於合格回料且兩者同為乾質量；超額回料另列存量。使用可用回料與設計斷面作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把全部粗料視為合格會低估新料，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「補充新道碴需求」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Fresh demand is required material minus qualified recovered material. In this model, demand is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 32.5 t. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Demand is at least qualified recovery and both are dry mass; surplus recovery is separate inventory. Use usable recovered material and required section as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Treating all coarse material as qualified understates fresh demand; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Fresh ballast requirement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：demand=95 t, recovered=72 t；y=demand-recovered=23 t。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: demand=95 t, recovered=72 t; y=demand-recovered=23 t.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把全部粗料視為合格會低估新料」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating all coarse material as qualified understates fresh demand.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「補充新道碴需求」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Fresh ballast requirement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-09-k1","title":"補充新道碴需求","titleEn":"Fresh ballast requirement","text":"需求扣除合格回料才得到新料需求。本模型把 demand 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 32.5 t。","textEn":"Fresh demand is required material minus qualified recovered material. In this model, demand is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把全部粗料視為合格會低估新料 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating all coarse material as qualified understates fresh demand. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「補充新道碴需求」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fresh ballast requirement\" is correct?","options":["需求扣除合格回料才得到新料需求。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把全部粗料視為合格會低估新料","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：混用濕基與乾基含水率會破壞物料平衡"],"optionsEn":["Fresh demand is required material minus qualified recovered material.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating all coarse material as qualified understates fresh demand.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing wet-basis and dry-basis moisture corrupts mass balance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"需求扣除合格回料才得到新料需求。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Fresh demand is required material minus qualified recovered material. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b344-v16-10","title":"補充新道碴需求：定量估算","titleEn":"Fresh ballast requirement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「補充新道碴需求」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fresh ballast requirement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：demand=95 t, recovered=72 t；y=demand-recovered=23 t。只把 demand 增加百分之十，y=32.5 t。模型邊界：需求不少於合格回料且兩者同為乾質量；超額回料另列存量；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: demand=95 t, recovered=72 t; y=demand-recovered=23 t. Increasing only demand with a ten-percent increase gives y=32.5 t. Boundary: Demand is at least qualified recovery and both are dry mass; surplus recovery is separate inventory; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以可用回料與設計斷面區分模型與觀察，先用設計材料需求、合格回料批號與乾質量帳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use usable recovered material and required section to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：demand=95 t, recovered=72 t；y=demand-recovered=23 t。只把 demand 增加百分之十，y=32.5 t。模型邊界：需求不少於合格回料且兩者同為乾質量；超額回料另列存量；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: demand=95 t, recovered=72 t; y=demand-recovered=23 t. Increasing only demand with a ten-percent increase gives y=32.5 t. Boundary: Demand is at least qualified recovery and both are dry mass; surplus recovery is separate inventory; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「補充新道碴需求」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fresh ballast requirement\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用岩石密度會低估運輸與暫存體積","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：demand=95 t, recovered=72 t；y=demand-recovered=23 t。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：不同取樣位置會被誤認為破碎增量"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Solid-rock density understates transport and storage volume.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: demand=95 t, recovered=72 t; y=demand-recovered=23 t.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Different sampling positions can imitate breakage growth."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：demand=95 t, recovered=72 t；y=demand-recovered=23 t。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: demand=95 t, recovered=72 t; y=demand-recovered=23 t. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b344-v16-11","title":"補充新道碴需求：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fresh ballast requirement: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「補充新道碴需求」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fresh ballast requirement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以可用回料與設計斷面區分模型與觀察，先用設計材料需求、合格回料批號與乾質量帳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「補充新道碴需求」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use usable recovered material and required section to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using required material quantity, qualified recovered batch IDs and dry-mass account, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Fresh ballast requirement. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「補充新道碴需求」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出需求不少於合格回料且兩者同為乾質量；超額回料另列存量如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把全部粗料視為合格會低估新料造成偏離的合成觀察，以可用回料與設計斷面說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Fresh ballast requirement, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Demand is at least qualified recovery and both are dry mass; surplus recovery is separate inventory. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Treating all coarse material as qualified understates fresh demand. Explain which evidence in usable recovered material and required section distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：把全部粗料視為合格會低估新料。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating all coarse material as qualified understates fresh demand. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以可用回料與設計斷面區分模型與觀察，先用設計材料需求、合格回料批號與乾質量帳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「補充新道碴需求」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use usable recovered material and required section to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using required material quantity, qualified recovered batch IDs and dry-mass account, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Fresh ballast requirement. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「補充新道碴需求」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出需求不少於合格回料且兩者同為乾質量；超額回料另列存量如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把全部粗料視為合格會低估新料造成偏離的合成觀察，以可用回料與設計斷面說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Fresh ballast requirement, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Demand is at least qualified recovery and both are dry mass; surplus recovery is separate inventory. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Treating all coarse material as qualified understates fresh demand. Explain which evidence in usable recovered material and required section distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「補充新道碴需求」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fresh ballast requirement\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把所有差額當成廢料會掩蓋量測問題","本單元以可用回料與設計斷面區分模型與觀察，先用設計材料需求、合格回料批號與乾質量帳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Labelling every discrepancy as waste hides measurement faults.","Use usable recovered material and required section to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以可用回料與設計斷面區分模型與觀察，先用設計材料需求、合格回料批號與乾質量帳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use usable recovered material and required section to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b344-v16-12","title":"補充新道碴需求：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fresh ballast requirement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「補充新道碴需求」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fresh ballast requirement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把全部粗料視為合格會低估新料。這個失效與「補充新道碴需求」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查可用回料與設計斷面，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating all coarse material as qualified understates fresh demand. This failure and a measurement bias in Fresh ballast requirement can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check usable recovered material and required section rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用可用回料與設計斷面作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把全部粗料視為合格會低估新料，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Treating all coarse material as qualified understates fresh demand; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把全部粗料視為合格會低估新料」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating all coarse material as qualified understates fresh demand.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把全部粗料視為合格會低估新料。這個失效與「補充新道碴需求」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查可用回料與設計斷面，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Treating all coarse material as qualified understates fresh demand. This failure and a measurement bias in Fresh ballast requirement can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check usable recovered material and required section rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「補充新道碴需求」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fresh ballast requirement\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把全部粗料視為合格會低估新料。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：混用濕基與乾基含水率會破壞物料平衡"],"optionsEn":["Treating all coarse material as qualified understates fresh demand.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing wet-basis and dry-basis moisture corrupts mass balance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把全部粗料視為合格會低估新料。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating all coarse material as qualified understates fresh demand. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b344-v16-13","title":"含水率乾重換算：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Moisture dry-mass conversion: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「含水率乾重換算」如何影響道碴清篩與再利用的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Moisture dry-mass conversion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ballast cleaning and reuse”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"含水率以乾質量為分母時，濕質量須除一加含水率。本模型把 wet 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 110 kg。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。含水率定義為水質量除乾料質量；水分分布具有代表性。使用濕重及乾燥後質量作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；混用濕基與乾基含水率會破壞物料平衡，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「含水率乾重換算」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For moisture content on a dry-mass basis, divide wet mass by one plus moisture ratio. In this model, wet is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 110 kg. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Moisture is water mass divided by dry-solid mass; sampled moisture is representative. Use wet mass and mass after drying as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Mixing wet-basis and dry-basis moisture corrupts mass balance; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Moisture dry-mass conversion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：wet=110 kg, w=0.1 1；y=wet/(1+w)=100 kg。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: wet=110 kg, w=0.1 1; y=wet/(1+w)=100 kg.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：混用濕基與乾基含水率會破壞物料平衡」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing wet-basis and dry-basis moisture corrupts mass balance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「含水率乾重換算」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Moisture dry-mass conversion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-13-k1","title":"含水率乾重換算","titleEn":"Moisture dry-mass conversion","text":"含水率以乾質量為分母時，濕質量須除一加含水率。本模型把 wet 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 110 kg。","textEn":"For moisture content on a dry-mass basis, divide wet mass by one plus moisture ratio. In this model, wet is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：混用濕基與乾基含水率會破壞物料平衡 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing wet-basis and dry-basis moisture corrupts mass balance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「含水率乾重換算」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Moisture dry-mass conversion\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：混用濕基與乾基含水率會破壞物料平衡","含水率以乾質量為分母時，濕質量須除一加含水率。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：篩網堵塞會讓細料被錯列為粗料"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing wet-basis and dry-basis moisture corrupts mass balance.","For moisture content on a dry-mass basis, divide wet mass by one plus moisture ratio.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Screen clogging misclassifies fines as coarse material."],"answer":1,"explanation":"含水率以乾質量為分母時，濕質量須除一加含水率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For moisture content on a dry-mass basis, divide wet mass by one plus moisture ratio. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b344-v16-14","title":"含水率乾重換算：定量估算","titleEn":"Moisture dry-mass conversion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「含水率乾重換算」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Moisture dry-mass conversion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：wet=110 kg, w=0.1 1；y=wet/(1+w)=100 kg。只把 wet 增加百分之十，y=110 kg。模型邊界：含水率定義為水質量除乾料質量；水分分布具有代表性；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: wet=110 kg, w=0.1 1; y=wet/(1+w)=100 kg. Increasing only wet with a ten-percent increase gives y=110 kg. Boundary: Moisture is water mass divided by dry-solid mass; sampled moisture is representative; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以濕重及乾燥後質量區分模型與觀察，先用同批濕重、乾燥後恆重及天平校準紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use wet mass and mass after drying to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：wet=110 kg, w=0.1 1；y=wet/(1+w)=100 kg。只把 wet 增加百分之十，y=110 kg。模型邊界：含水率定義為水質量除乾料質量；水分分布具有代表性；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: wet=110 kg, w=0.1 1; y=wet/(1+w)=100 kg. Increasing only wet with a ten-percent increase gives y=110 kg. Boundary: Moisture is water mass divided by dry-solid mass; sampled moisture is representative; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「含水率乾重換算」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Moisture dry-mass conversion\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：短時峰值不代表整班處理量","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：空氣滯留會使初期流量不能代表穩態","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：wet=110 kg, w=0.1 1；y=wet/(1+w)=100 kg。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A short peak rate does not represent shift production.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Trapped air makes initial flow unrepresentative of steady flow.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: wet=110 kg, w=0.1 1; y=wet/(1+w)=100 kg."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：wet=110 kg, w=0.1 1；y=wet/(1+w)=100 kg。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: wet=110 kg, w=0.1 1; y=wet/(1+w)=100 kg. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b344-v16-15","title":"含水率乾重換算：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Moisture dry-mass conversion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「含水率乾重換算」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Moisture dry-mass conversion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以濕重及乾燥後質量區分模型與觀察，先用同批濕重、乾燥後恆重及天平校準紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「含水率乾重換算」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use wet mass and mass after drying to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using wet mass and constant dry mass from one batch plus balance calibration, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Moisture dry-mass conversion. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「含水率乾重換算」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出含水率定義為水質量除乾料質量；水分分布具有代表性如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由混用濕基與乾基含水率會破壞物料平衡造成偏離的合成觀察，以濕重及乾燥後質量說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Moisture dry-mass conversion, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Moisture is water mass divided by dry-solid mass; sampled moisture is representative. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Mixing wet-basis and dry-basis moisture corrupts mass balance. Explain which evidence in wet mass and mass after drying distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：混用濕基與乾基含水率會破壞物料平衡。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mixing wet-basis and dry-basis moisture corrupts mass balance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以濕重及乾燥後質量區分模型與觀察，先用同批濕重、乾燥後恆重及天平校準紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「含水率乾重換算」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use wet mass and mass after drying to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using wet mass and constant dry mass from one batch plus balance calibration, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Moisture dry-mass conversion. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「含水率乾重換算」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出含水率定義為水質量除乾料質量；水分分布具有代表性如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由混用濕基與乾基含水率會破壞物料平衡造成偏離的合成觀察，以濕重及乾燥後質量說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Moisture dry-mass conversion, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Moisture is water mass divided by dry-solid mass; sampled moisture is representative. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Mixing wet-basis and dry-basis moisture corrupts mass balance. Explain which evidence in wet mass and mass after drying distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「含水率乾重換算」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Moisture dry-mass conversion\"?","options":["本單元以濕重及乾燥後質量區分模型與觀察，先用同批濕重、乾燥後恆重及天平校準紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未記錄存料會把正常暫存當成損耗"],"optionsEn":["Use wet mass and mass after drying to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Unrecorded inventory makes temporary storage appear as loss."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以濕重及乾燥後質量區分模型與觀察，先用同批濕重、乾燥後恆重及天平校準紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use wet mass and mass after drying to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b344-v16-16","title":"含水率乾重換算：失效診斷","titleEn":"Moisture dry-mass conversion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「含水率乾重換算」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Moisture dry-mass conversion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"混用濕基與乾基含水率會破壞物料平衡。這個失效與「含水率乾重換算」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查濕重及乾燥後質量，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mixing wet-basis and dry-basis moisture corrupts mass balance. This failure and a measurement bias in Moisture dry-mass conversion can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check wet mass and mass after drying rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用濕重及乾燥後質量作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；混用濕基與乾基含水率會破壞物料平衡，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Mixing wet-basis and dry-basis moisture corrupts mass balance; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：混用濕基與乾基含水率會破壞物料平衡」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing wet-basis and dry-basis moisture corrupts mass balance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"混用濕基與乾基含水率會破壞物料平衡。這個失效與「含水率乾重換算」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查濕重及乾燥後質量，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Mixing wet-basis and dry-basis moisture corrupts mass balance. This failure and a measurement bias in Moisture dry-mass conversion can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check wet mass and mass after drying rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「含水率乾重換算」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Moisture dry-mass conversion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","混用濕基與乾基含水率會破壞物料平衡。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：篩網堵塞會讓細料被錯列為粗料"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Mixing wet-basis and dry-basis moisture corrupts mass balance.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Screen clogging misclassifies fines as coarse material."],"answer":1,"explanation":"混用濕基與乾基含水率會破壞物料平衡。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mixing wet-basis and dry-basis moisture corrupts mass balance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b344-v16-s3","title":"篩分通過比例與散裝體積換算","titleEn":"Sieve passing fraction & Bulk-volume conversion","description":"本階段聚焦「篩分通過比例」與「散裝體積換算」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Sieve passing fraction\" and \"Bulk-volume conversion\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b344-v16-17","title":"篩分通過比例：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Sieve passing fraction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「篩分通過比例」如何影響道碴清篩與再利用的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sieve passing fraction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ballast cleaning and reuse”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"通過質量除樣本乾重描述指定篩級。本模型把 passing 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 16.5 percent。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。通過量與樣本量皆為同批乾質量；只代表一個篩級。使用篩前篩後稱量作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；篩網堵塞會讓細料被錯列為粗料，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「篩分通過比例」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Passing mass divided by sample dry mass describes one specified sieve class. In this model, passing is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 16.5 percent. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Passing and sample amounts are dry masses from one batch; only one sieve class is represented. Use weighing before and after sieving as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Screen clogging misclassifies fines as coarse material; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Sieve passing fraction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：passing=18 kg, sample=120 kg；y=passing/sample*100=15 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: passing=18 kg, sample=120 kg; y=passing/sample*100=15 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：篩網堵塞會讓細料被錯列為粗料」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Screen clogging misclassifies fines as coarse material.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「篩分通過比例」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Sieve passing fraction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-17-k1","title":"篩分通過比例","titleEn":"Sieve passing fraction","text":"通過質量除樣本乾重描述指定篩級。本模型把 passing 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 16.5 percent。","textEn":"Passing mass divided by sample dry mass describes one specified sieve class. In this model, passing is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：篩網堵塞會讓細料被錯列為粗料 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Screen clogging misclassifies fines as coarse material. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「篩分通過比例」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Sieve passing fraction\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：篩網堵塞會讓細料被錯列為粗料","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用岩石密度會低估運輸與暫存體積","通過質量除樣本乾重描述指定篩級。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Screen clogging misclassifies fines as coarse material.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Solid-rock density understates transport and storage volume.","Passing mass divided by sample dry mass describes one specified sieve class."],"answer":2,"explanation":"通過質量除樣本乾重描述指定篩級。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Passing mass divided by sample dry mass describes one specified sieve class. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b344-v16-18","title":"篩分通過比例：定量估算","titleEn":"Sieve passing fraction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「篩分通過比例」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sieve passing fraction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：passing=18 kg, sample=120 kg；y=passing/sample*100=15 percent。只把 passing 增加百分之十，y=16.5 percent。模型邊界：通過量與樣本量皆為同批乾質量；只代表一個篩級；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: passing=18 kg, sample=120 kg; y=passing/sample*100=15 percent. Increasing only passing with a ten-percent increase gives y=16.5 percent. Boundary: Passing and sample amounts are dry masses from one batch; only one sieve class is represented; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以篩前篩後稱量區分模型與觀察，先用篩前樣本重、各篩留存重及質量閉合差建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use weighing before and after sieving to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：passing=18 kg, sample=120 kg；y=passing/sample*100=15 percent。只把 passing 增加百分之十，y=16.5 percent。模型邊界：通過量與樣本量皆為同批乾質量；只代表一個篩級；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: passing=18 kg, sample=120 kg; y=passing/sample*100=15 percent. Increasing only passing with a ten-percent increase gives y=16.5 percent. Boundary: Passing and sample amounts are dry masses from one batch; only one sieve class is represented; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「篩分通過比例」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Sieve passing fraction\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：passing=18 kg, sample=120 kg；y=passing/sample*100=15 percent。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：不同取樣位置會被誤認為破碎增量","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把所有差額當成廢料會掩蓋量測問題"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: passing=18 kg, sample=120 kg; y=passing/sample*100=15 percent.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Different sampling positions can imitate breakage growth.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Labelling every discrepancy as waste hides measurement faults."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：passing=18 kg, sample=120 kg；y=passing/sample*100=15 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: passing=18 kg, sample=120 kg; y=passing/sample*100=15 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b344-v16-19","title":"篩分通過比例：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Sieve passing fraction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「篩分通過比例」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Sieve passing fraction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以篩前篩後稱量區分模型與觀察，先用篩前樣本重、各篩留存重及質量閉合差建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「篩分通過比例」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use weighing before and after sieving to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using initial sample mass, mass retained on each sieve and mass-closure residual, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Sieve passing fraction. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「篩分通過比例」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出通過量與樣本量皆為同批乾質量；只代表一個篩級如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由篩網堵塞會讓細料被錯列為粗料造成偏離的合成觀察，以篩前篩後稱量說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Sieve passing fraction, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Passing and sample amounts are dry masses from one batch; only one sieve class is represented. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Screen clogging misclassifies fines as coarse material. Explain which evidence in weighing before and after sieving distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：篩網堵塞會讓細料被錯列為粗料。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Screen clogging misclassifies fines as coarse material. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以篩前篩後稱量區分模型與觀察，先用篩前樣本重、各篩留存重及質量閉合差建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「篩分通過比例」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use weighing before and after sieving to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using initial sample mass, mass retained on each sieve and mass-closure residual, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Sieve passing fraction. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「篩分通過比例」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出通過量與樣本量皆為同批乾質量；只代表一個篩級如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由篩網堵塞會讓細料被錯列為粗料造成偏離的合成觀察，以篩前篩後稱量說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Sieve passing fraction, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Passing and sample amounts are dry masses from one batch; only one sieve class is represented. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Screen clogging misclassifies fines as coarse material. Explain which evidence in weighing before and after sieving distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「篩分通過比例」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Sieve passing fraction\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","本單元以篩前篩後稱量區分模型與觀察，先用篩前樣本重、各篩留存重及質量閉合差建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：高回收率也可能保留脆弱顆粒"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Use weighing before and after sieving to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A high recovery fraction may retain weak particles."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以篩前篩後稱量區分模型與觀察，先用篩前樣本重、各篩留存重及質量閉合差建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use weighing before and after sieving to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b344-v16-20","title":"篩分通過比例：失效診斷","titleEn":"Sieve passing fraction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「篩分通過比例」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Sieve passing fraction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"篩網堵塞會讓細料被錯列為粗料。這個失效與「篩分通過比例」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查篩前篩後稱量，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Screen clogging misclassifies fines as coarse material. This failure and a measurement bias in Sieve passing fraction can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check weighing before and after sieving rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用篩前篩後稱量作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；篩網堵塞會讓細料被錯列為粗料，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Screen clogging misclassifies fines as coarse material; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：篩網堵塞會讓細料被錯列為粗料」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Screen clogging misclassifies fines as coarse material.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"篩網堵塞會讓細料被錯列為粗料。這個失效與「篩分通過比例」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查篩前篩後稱量，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Screen clogging misclassifies fines as coarse material. This failure and a measurement bias in Sieve passing fraction can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check weighing before and after sieving rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「篩分通過比例」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Sieve passing fraction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用岩石密度會低估運輸與暫存體積","篩網堵塞會讓細料被錯列為粗料。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Solid-rock density understates transport and storage volume.","Screen clogging misclassifies fines as coarse material."],"answer":2,"explanation":"篩網堵塞會讓細料被錯列為粗料。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Screen clogging misclassifies fines as coarse material. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b344-v16-21","title":"散裝體積換算：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bulk-volume conversion: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「散裝體積換算」如何影響道碴清篩與再利用的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Bulk-volume conversion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ballast cleaning and reuse”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"散裝密度包含顆粒間空隙，不能改用岩石本體密度。本模型把 mass 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 27.5 m3。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。散裝密度適用同含水率及堆積狀態；不使用岩石本體密度。使用料斗體積與質量作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；用岩石密度會低估運輸與暫存體積，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「散裝體積換算」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Bulk density includes interparticle voids and cannot be replaced by solid-rock density. In this model, mass is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 27.5 m3. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Bulk density applies to the same moisture and packing state; solid-rock density is not used. Use hopper volume and mass as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Solid-rock density understates transport and storage volume; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Bulk-volume conversion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：mass=40 t, bulk=1.6 t/m3；y=mass/bulk=25 m3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: mass=40 t, bulk=1.6 t/m3; y=mass/bulk=25 m3.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用岩石密度會低估運輸與暫存體積」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Solid-rock density understates transport and storage volume.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「散裝體積換算」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Bulk-volume conversion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-21-k1","title":"散裝體積換算","titleEn":"Bulk-volume conversion","text":"散裝密度包含顆粒間空隙，不能改用岩石本體密度。本模型把 mass 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 27.5 m3。","textEn":"Bulk density includes interparticle voids and cannot be replaced by solid-rock density. In this model, mass is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用岩石密度會低估運輸與暫存體積 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Solid-rock density understates transport and storage volume. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「散裝體積換算」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bulk-volume conversion\" is correct?","options":["散裝密度包含顆粒間空隙，不能改用岩石本體密度。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用岩石密度會低估運輸與暫存體積","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：短時峰值不代表整班處理量"],"optionsEn":["Bulk density includes interparticle voids and cannot be replaced by solid-rock density.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Solid-rock density understates transport and storage volume.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A short peak rate does not represent shift production."],"answer":0,"explanation":"散裝密度包含顆粒間空隙，不能改用岩石本體密度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Bulk density includes interparticle voids and cannot be replaced by solid-rock density. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b344-v16-22","title":"散裝體積換算：定量估算","titleEn":"Bulk-volume conversion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「散裝體積換算」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Bulk-volume conversion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：mass=40 t, bulk=1.6 t/m3；y=mass/bulk=25 m3。只把 mass 增加百分之十，y=27.5 m3。模型邊界：散裝密度適用同含水率及堆積狀態；不使用岩石本體密度；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: mass=40 t, bulk=1.6 t/m3; y=mass/bulk=25 m3. Increasing only mass with a ten-percent increase gives y=27.5 m3. Boundary: Bulk density applies to the same moisture and packing state; solid-rock density is not used; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以料斗體積與質量區分模型與觀察，先用已知容積容器、批次秤重及堆積狀態影像建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use hopper volume and mass to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：mass=40 t, bulk=1.6 t/m3；y=mass/bulk=25 m3。只把 mass 增加百分之十，y=27.5 m3。模型邊界：散裝密度適用同含水率及堆積狀態；不使用岩石本體密度；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: mass=40 t, bulk=1.6 t/m3; y=mass/bulk=25 m3. Increasing only mass with a ten-percent increase gives y=27.5 m3. Boundary: Bulk density applies to the same moisture and packing state; solid-rock density is not used; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「散裝體積換算」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bulk-volume conversion\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：空氣滯留會使初期流量不能代表穩態","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：mass=40 t, bulk=1.6 t/m3；y=mass/bulk=25 m3。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未記錄存料會把正常暫存當成損耗"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Trapped air makes initial flow unrepresentative of steady flow.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: mass=40 t, bulk=1.6 t/m3; y=mass/bulk=25 m3.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Unrecorded inventory makes temporary storage appear as loss."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：mass=40 t, bulk=1.6 t/m3；y=mass/bulk=25 m3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: mass=40 t, bulk=1.6 t/m3; y=mass/bulk=25 m3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b344-v16-23","title":"散裝體積換算：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bulk-volume conversion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「散裝體積換算」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Bulk-volume conversion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以料斗體積與質量區分模型與觀察，先用已知容積容器、批次秤重及堆積狀態影像建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「散裝體積換算」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use hopper volume and mass to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using known-volume container, batch weighing and packing-state images, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Bulk-volume conversion. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「散裝體積換算」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出散裝密度適用同含水率及堆積狀態；不使用岩石本體密度如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由用岩石密度會低估運輸與暫存體積造成偏離的合成觀察，以料斗體積與質量說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Bulk-volume conversion, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Bulk density applies to the same moisture and packing state; solid-rock density is not used. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Solid-rock density understates transport and storage volume. Explain which evidence in hopper volume and mass distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：用岩石密度會低估運輸與暫存體積。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Solid-rock density understates transport and storage volume. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以料斗體積與質量區分模型與觀察，先用已知容積容器、批次秤重及堆積狀態影像建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「散裝體積換算」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use hopper volume and mass to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using known-volume container, batch weighing and packing-state images, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Bulk-volume conversion. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「散裝體積換算」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出散裝密度適用同含水率及堆積狀態；不使用岩石本體密度如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由用岩石密度會低估運輸與暫存體積造成偏離的合成觀察，以料斗體積與質量說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Bulk-volume conversion, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Bulk density applies to the same moisture and packing state; solid-rock density is not used. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Solid-rock density understates transport and storage volume. Explain which evidence in hopper volume and mass distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「散裝體積換算」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bulk-volume conversion\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把全部粗料視為合格會低估新料","本單元以料斗體積與質量區分模型與觀察，先用已知容積容器、批次秤重及堆積狀態影像建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating all coarse material as qualified understates fresh demand.","Use hopper volume and mass to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以料斗體積與質量區分模型與觀察，先用已知容積容器、批次秤重及堆積狀態影像建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use hopper volume and mass to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b344-v16-24","title":"散裝體積換算：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bulk-volume conversion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「散裝體積換算」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Bulk-volume conversion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用岩石密度會低估運輸與暫存體積。這個失效與「散裝體積換算」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查料斗體積與質量，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Solid-rock density understates transport and storage volume. This failure and a measurement bias in Bulk-volume conversion can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check hopper volume and mass rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用料斗體積與質量作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；用岩石密度會低估運輸與暫存體積，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Solid-rock density understates transport and storage volume; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用岩石密度會低估運輸與暫存體積」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Solid-rock density understates transport and storage volume.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用岩石密度會低估運輸與暫存體積。這個失效與「散裝體積換算」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查料斗體積與質量，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Solid-rock density understates transport and storage volume. This failure and a measurement bias in Bulk-volume conversion can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check hopper volume and mass rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「散裝體積換算」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bulk-volume conversion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["用岩石密度會低估運輸與暫存體積。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：短時峰值不代表整班處理量"],"optionsEn":["Solid-rock density understates transport and storage volume.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A short peak rate does not represent shift production."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用岩石密度會低估運輸與暫存體積。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Solid-rock density understates transport and storage volume. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b344-v16-s4","title":"清篩處理速率與細料新增損傷","titleEn":"Screening throughput & New fines from breakage","description":"本階段聚焦「清篩處理速率」與「細料新增損傷」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Screening throughput\" and \"New fines from breakage\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b344-v16-25","title":"清篩處理速率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Screening throughput: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「清篩處理速率」如何影響道碴清篩與再利用的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Screening throughput” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ballast cleaning and reuse”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"物料處理率需明確時間窗並扣除等待。本模型把 mass 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 176 t/h。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。質量與時間窗一致；說明時間是否包含等待與維修。使用連續秤重與運轉時間作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；短時峰值不代表整班處理量，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「清篩處理速率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Processing rate needs a defined time window and treatment of waiting. In this model, mass is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 176 t/h. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Mass and time window agree; state whether waiting and maintenance are included. Use continuous weighing and operating time as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. A short peak rate does not represent shift production; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Screening throughput” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：mass=80 t, time=0.5 h；y=mass/time=160 t/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: mass=80 t, time=0.5 h; y=mass/time=160 t/h.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：短時峰值不代表整班處理量」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A short peak rate does not represent shift production.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「清篩處理速率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Screening throughput”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-25-k1","title":"清篩處理速率","titleEn":"Screening throughput","text":"物料處理率需明確時間窗並扣除等待。本模型把 mass 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 176 t/h。","textEn":"Processing rate needs a defined time window and treatment of waiting. In this model, mass is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：短時峰值不代表整班處理量 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A short peak rate does not represent shift production. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「清篩處理速率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Screening throughput\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：短時峰值不代表整班處理量","物料處理率需明確時間窗並扣除等待。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：不同取樣位置會被誤認為破碎增量"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A short peak rate does not represent shift production.","Processing rate needs a defined time window and treatment of waiting.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Different sampling positions can imitate breakage growth."],"answer":1,"explanation":"物料處理率需明確時間窗並扣除等待。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Processing rate needs a defined time window and treatment of waiting. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b344-v16-26","title":"清篩處理速率：定量估算","titleEn":"Screening throughput: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「清篩處理速率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Screening throughput” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：mass=80 t, time=0.5 h；y=mass/time=160 t/h。只把 mass 增加百分之十，y=176 t/h。模型邊界：質量與時間窗一致；說明時間是否包含等待與維修；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: mass=80 t, time=0.5 h; y=mass/time=160 t/h. Increasing only mass with a ten-percent increase gives y=176 t/h. Boundary: Mass and time window agree; state whether waiting and maintenance are included; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以連續秤重與運轉時間區分模型與觀察，先用連續皮帶秤、起訖時間戳與設備狀態記錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use continuous weighing and operating time to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：mass=80 t, time=0.5 h；y=mass/time=160 t/h。只把 mass 增加百分之十，y=176 t/h。模型邊界：質量與時間窗一致；說明時間是否包含等待與維修；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: mass=80 t, time=0.5 h; y=mass/time=160 t/h. Increasing only mass with a ten-percent increase gives y=176 t/h. Boundary: Mass and time window agree; state whether waiting and maintenance are included; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「清篩處理速率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Screening throughput\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把所有差額當成廢料會掩蓋量測問題","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：高回收率也可能保留脆弱顆粒","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：mass=80 t, time=0.5 h；y=mass/time=160 t/h。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Labelling every discrepancy as waste hides measurement faults.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A high recovery fraction may retain weak particles.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: mass=80 t, time=0.5 h; y=mass/time=160 t/h."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：mass=80 t, time=0.5 h；y=mass/time=160 t/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: mass=80 t, time=0.5 h; y=mass/time=160 t/h. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b344-v16-27","title":"清篩處理速率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Screening throughput: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「清篩處理速率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Screening throughput” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以連續秤重與運轉時間區分模型與觀察，先用連續皮帶秤、起訖時間戳與設備狀態記錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「清篩處理速率」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use continuous weighing and operating time to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using continuous belt-scale readings, start-end timestamps and equipment-state log, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Screening throughput. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「清篩處理速率」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出質量與時間窗一致；說明時間是否包含等待與維修如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由短時峰值不代表整班處理量造成偏離的合成觀察，以連續秤重與運轉時間說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Screening throughput, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Mass and time window agree; state whether waiting and maintenance are included. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A short peak rate does not represent shift production. Explain which evidence in continuous weighing and operating time distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：短時峰值不代表整班處理量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A short peak rate does not represent shift production. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以連續秤重與運轉時間區分模型與觀察，先用連續皮帶秤、起訖時間戳與設備狀態記錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「清篩處理速率」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use continuous weighing and operating time to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using continuous belt-scale readings, start-end timestamps and equipment-state log, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Screening throughput. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「清篩處理速率」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出質量與時間窗一致；說明時間是否包含等待與維修如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由短時峰值不代表整班處理量造成偏離的合成觀察，以連續秤重與運轉時間說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Screening throughput, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Mass and time window agree; state whether waiting and maintenance are included. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A short peak rate does not represent shift production. Explain which evidence in continuous weighing and operating time distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「清篩處理速率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Screening throughput\"?","options":["本單元以連續秤重與運轉時間區分模型與觀察，先用連續皮帶秤、起訖時間戳與設備狀態記錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：混用濕基與乾基含水率會破壞物料平衡"],"optionsEn":["Use continuous weighing and operating time to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing wet-basis and dry-basis moisture corrupts mass balance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以連續秤重與運轉時間區分模型與觀察，先用連續皮帶秤、起訖時間戳與設備狀態記錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use continuous weighing and operating time to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b344-v16-28","title":"清篩處理速率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Screening throughput: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「清篩處理速率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Screening throughput” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"短時峰值不代表整班處理量。這個失效與「清篩處理速率」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查連續秤重與運轉時間，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A short peak rate does not represent shift production. This failure and a measurement bias in Screening throughput can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check continuous weighing and operating time rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用連續秤重與運轉時間作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；短時峰值不代表整班處理量，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A short peak rate does not represent shift production; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：短時峰值不代表整班處理量」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A short peak rate does not represent shift production.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"短時峰值不代表整班處理量。這個失效與「清篩處理速率」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查連續秤重與運轉時間，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"A short peak rate does not represent shift production. This failure and a measurement bias in Screening throughput can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check continuous weighing and operating time rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「清篩處理速率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Screening throughput\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","短時峰值不代表整班處理量。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：不同取樣位置會被誤認為破碎增量"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A short peak rate does not represent shift production.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Different sampling positions can imitate breakage growth."],"answer":1,"explanation":"短時峰值不代表整班處理量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A short peak rate does not represent shift production. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b344-v16-29","title":"細料新增損傷：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"New fines from breakage: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「細料新增損傷」如何影響道碴清篩與再利用的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “New fines from breakage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ballast cleaning and reuse”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"前後細料差可檢查清篩過程是否產生額外破碎。本模型把 before 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出減少為 3.5 percent。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。前後樣本來自同批並使用同一篩界；沒有外來細料加入。使用同批料前後粒徑作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；不同取樣位置會被誤認為破碎增量，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「細料新增損傷」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Change in fines checks whether processing generated additional breakage. In this model, before is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output decreases to 3.5 percent. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Before-after samples share a batch and sieve boundary; no external fines are added. Use before-and-after grading of the same batch as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Different sampling positions can imitate breakage growth; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “New fines from breakage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：before=5 kg, after=9 kg, total=100 kg；y=(after-before)/total*100=4 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: before=5 kg, after=9 kg, total=100 kg; y=(after-before)/total*100=4 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：不同取樣位置會被誤認為破碎增量」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Different sampling positions can imitate breakage growth.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「細料新增損傷」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “New fines from breakage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-29-k1","title":"細料新增損傷","titleEn":"New fines from breakage","text":"前後細料差可檢查清篩過程是否產生額外破碎。本模型把 before 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出減少為 3.5 percent。","textEn":"Change in fines checks whether processing generated additional breakage. In this model, before is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：不同取樣位置會被誤認為破碎增量 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Different sampling positions can imitate breakage growth. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「細料新增損傷」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"New fines from breakage\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：不同取樣位置會被誤認為破碎增量","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：空氣滯留會使初期流量不能代表穩態","前後細料差可檢查清篩過程是否產生額外破碎。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Different sampling positions can imitate breakage growth.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Trapped air makes initial flow unrepresentative of steady flow.","Change in fines checks whether processing generated additional breakage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"前後細料差可檢查清篩過程是否產生額外破碎。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Change in fines checks whether processing generated additional breakage. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b344-v16-30","title":"細料新增損傷：定量估算","titleEn":"New fines from breakage: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「細料新增損傷」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “New fines from breakage” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：before=5 kg, after=9 kg, total=100 kg；y=(after-before)/total*100=4 percent。只把 before 增加百分之十，y=3.5 percent。模型邊界：前後樣本來自同批並使用同一篩界；沒有外來細料加入；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: before=5 kg, after=9 kg, total=100 kg; y=(after-before)/total*100=4 percent. Increasing only before with a ten-percent increase gives y=3.5 percent. Boundary: Before-after samples share a batch and sieve boundary; no external fines are added; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以同批料前後粒徑區分模型與觀察，先用配對樣本的乾重粒徑分布及取樣位置建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use before-and-after grading of the same batch to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：before=5 kg, after=9 kg, total=100 kg；y=(after-before)/total*100=4 percent。只把 before 增加百分之十，y=3.5 percent。模型邊界：前後樣本來自同批並使用同一篩界；沒有外來細料加入；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: before=5 kg, after=9 kg, total=100 kg; y=(after-before)/total*100=4 percent. Increasing only before with a ten-percent increase gives y=3.5 percent. Boundary: Before-after samples share a batch and sieve boundary; no external fines are added; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「細料新增損傷」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"New fines from breakage\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：before=5 kg, after=9 kg, total=100 kg。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未記錄存料會把正常暫存當成損耗","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把全部粗料視為合格會低估新料"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: before=5 kg, after=9 kg, total=100 kg; y=(after-before)/total*100=4 percent.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Unrecorded inventory makes temporary storage appear as loss.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating all coarse material as qualified understates fresh demand."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：before=5 kg, after=9 kg, total=100 kg；y=(after-before)/total*100=4 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: before=5 kg, after=9 kg, total=100 kg; y=(after-before)/total*100=4 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b344-v16-31","title":"細料新增損傷：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"New fines from breakage: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「細料新增損傷」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “New fines from breakage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以同批料前後粒徑區分模型與觀察，先用配對樣本的乾重粒徑分布及取樣位置建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「細料新增損傷」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use before-and-after grading of the same batch to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using paired dry-mass grading distributions and sample locations, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by New fines from breakage. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「細料新增損傷」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出前後樣本來自同批並使用同一篩界；沒有外來細料加入如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由不同取樣位置會被誤認為破碎增量造成偏離的合成觀察，以同批料前後粒徑說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for New fines from breakage, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Before-after samples share a batch and sieve boundary; no external fines are added. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Different sampling positions can imitate breakage growth. Explain which evidence in before-and-after grading of the same batch distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：不同取樣位置會被誤認為破碎增量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Different sampling positions can imitate breakage growth. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以同批料前後粒徑區分模型與觀察，先用配對樣本的乾重粒徑分布及取樣位置建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「細料新增損傷」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use before-and-after grading of the same batch to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using paired dry-mass grading distributions and sample locations, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by New fines from breakage. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「細料新增損傷」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出前後樣本來自同批並使用同一篩界；沒有外來細料加入如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由不同取樣位置會被誤認為破碎增量造成偏離的合成觀察，以同批料前後粒徑說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for New fines from breakage, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Before-after samples share a batch and sieve boundary; no external fines are added. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Different sampling positions can imitate breakage growth. Explain which evidence in before-and-after grading of the same batch distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「細料新增損傷」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"New fines from breakage\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以同批料前後粒徑區分模型與觀察，先用配對樣本的乾重粒徑分布及取樣位置建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：篩網堵塞會讓細料被錯列為粗料"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use before-and-after grading of the same batch to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Screen clogging misclassifies fines as coarse material."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以同批料前後粒徑區分模型與觀察，先用配對樣本的乾重粒徑分布及取樣位置建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use before-and-after grading of the same batch to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b344-v16-32","title":"細料新增損傷：失效診斷","titleEn":"New fines from breakage: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「細料新增損傷」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “New fines from breakage” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"不同取樣位置會被誤認為破碎增量。這個失效與「細料新增損傷」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查同批料前後粒徑，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Different sampling positions can imitate breakage growth. This failure and a measurement bias in New fines from breakage can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check before-and-after grading of the same batch rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用同批料前後粒徑作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；不同取樣位置會被誤認為破碎增量，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Different sampling positions can imitate breakage growth; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：不同取樣位置會被誤認為破碎增量」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Different sampling positions can imitate breakage growth.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"不同取樣位置會被誤認為破碎增量。這個失效與「細料新增損傷」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查同批料前後粒徑，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Different sampling positions can imitate breakage growth. This failure and a measurement bias in New fines from breakage can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check before-and-after grading of the same batch rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「細料新增損傷」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"New fines from breakage\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：空氣滯留會使初期流量不能代表穩態","不同取樣位置會被誤認為破碎增量。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Trapped air makes initial flow unrepresentative of steady flow.","Different sampling positions can imitate breakage growth."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同取樣位置會被誤認為破碎增量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Different sampling positions can imitate breakage growth. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b344-v16-s5","title":"滲透流量比較與未回收物料比例","titleEn":"Permeability flow comparison & Unrecovered material fraction","description":"本階段聚焦「滲透流量比較」與「未回收物料比例」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Permeability flow comparison\" and \"Unrecovered material fraction\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b344-v16-33","title":"滲透流量比較：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Permeability flow comparison: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「滲透流量比較」如何影響道碴清篩與再利用的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Permeability flow comparison” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ballast cleaning and reuse”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"流量反算滲透率須記錄水力梯度與試體斷面。本模型把 Q 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.011 m/s。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。飽和穩態達西滲流且無側漏；結果是試體等效滲透率。使用水頭與流量穩定區段作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；空氣滯留會使初期流量不能代表穩態，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「滲透流量比較」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Inferring permeability from flow requires hydraulic gradient and specimen area. In this model, Q is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 0.011 m/s. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Saturated steady Darcy flow without side leakage; the result is specimen-equivalent permeability. Use stable intervals of head and flow as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Trapped air makes initial flow unrepresentative of steady flow; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Permeability flow comparison” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：Q=0.0001 m3/s, A=0.02 m2, i=0.5 1；y=Q/(A*i)=0.01 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: Q=0.0001 m3/s, A=0.02 m2, i=0.5 1; y=Q/(A*i)=0.01 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：空氣滯留會使初期流量不能代表穩態」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Trapped air makes initial flow unrepresentative of steady flow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「滲透流量比較」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Permeability flow comparison”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-33-k1","title":"滲透流量比較","titleEn":"Permeability flow comparison","text":"流量反算滲透率須記錄水力梯度與試體斷面。本模型把 Q 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.011 m/s。","textEn":"Inferring permeability from flow requires hydraulic gradient and specimen area. In this model, Q is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：空氣滯留會使初期流量不能代表穩態 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Trapped air makes initial flow unrepresentative of steady flow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「滲透流量比較」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Permeability flow comparison\" is correct?","options":["流量反算滲透率須記錄水力梯度與試體斷面。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：空氣滯留會使初期流量不能代表穩態","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把所有差額當成廢料會掩蓋量測問題"],"optionsEn":["Inferring permeability from flow requires hydraulic gradient and specimen area.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Trapped air makes initial flow unrepresentative of steady flow.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Labelling every discrepancy as waste hides measurement faults."],"answer":0,"explanation":"流量反算滲透率須記錄水力梯度與試體斷面。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Inferring permeability from flow requires hydraulic gradient and specimen area. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b344-v16-34","title":"滲透流量比較：定量估算","titleEn":"Permeability flow comparison: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「滲透流量比較」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Permeability flow comparison” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：Q=0.0001 m3/s, A=0.02 m2, i=0.5 1；y=Q/(A*i)=0.01 m/s。只把 Q 增加百分之十，y=0.011 m/s。模型邊界：飽和穩態達西滲流且無側漏；結果是試體等效滲透率；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: Q=0.0001 m3/s, A=0.02 m2, i=0.5 1; y=Q/(A*i)=0.01 m/s. Increasing only Q with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.011 m/s. Boundary: Saturated steady Darcy flow without side leakage; the result is specimen-equivalent permeability; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以水頭與流量穩定區段區分模型與觀察，先用穩定水頭時間序列、試體斷面與定時排水量建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use stable intervals of head and flow to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：Q=0.0001 m3/s, A=0.02 m2, i=0.5 1；y=Q/(A*i)=0.01 m/s。只把 Q 增加百分之十，y=0.011 m/s。模型邊界：飽和穩態達西滲流且無側漏；結果是試體等效滲透率；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: Q=0.0001 m3/s, A=0.02 m2, i=0.5 1; y=Q/(A*i)=0.01 m/s. Increasing only Q with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.011 m/s. Boundary: Saturated steady Darcy flow without side leakage; the result is specimen-equivalent permeability; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「滲透流量比較」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Permeability flow comparison\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：高回收率也可能保留脆弱顆粒","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：Q=0.0001 m3/s, A=0.02 m2, i=0.5 1；y=Q/(A*i)=0.01 m/s。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：混用濕基與乾基含水率會破壞物料平衡"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A high recovery fraction may retain weak particles.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: Q=0.0001 m3/s, A=0.02 m2, i=0.5 1; y=Q/(A*i)=0.01 m/s.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing wet-basis and dry-basis moisture corrupts mass balance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：Q=0.0001 m3/s, A=0.02 m2, i=0.5 1；y=Q/(A*i)=0.01 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: Q=0.0001 m3/s, A=0.02 m2, i=0.5 1; y=Q/(A*i)=0.01 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b344-v16-35","title":"滲透流量比較：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Permeability flow comparison: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「滲透流量比較」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Permeability flow comparison” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以水頭與流量穩定區段區分模型與觀察，先用穩定水頭時間序列、試體斷面與定時排水量建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「滲透流量比較」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use stable intervals of head and flow to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using stable head history, specimen area and timed discharge volume, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Permeability flow comparison. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「滲透流量比較」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出飽和穩態達西滲流且無側漏；結果是試體等效滲透率如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由空氣滯留會使初期流量不能代表穩態造成偏離的合成觀察，以水頭與流量穩定區段說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Permeability flow comparison, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Saturated steady Darcy flow without side leakage; the result is specimen-equivalent permeability. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Trapped air makes initial flow unrepresentative of steady flow. Explain which evidence in stable intervals of head and flow distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：空氣滯留會使初期流量不能代表穩態。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Trapped air makes initial flow unrepresentative of steady flow. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以水頭與流量穩定區段區分模型與觀察，先用穩定水頭時間序列、試體斷面與定時排水量建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「滲透流量比較」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use stable intervals of head and flow to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using stable head history, specimen area and timed discharge volume, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Permeability flow comparison. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「滲透流量比較」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出飽和穩態達西滲流且無側漏；結果是試體等效滲透率如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由空氣滯留會使初期流量不能代表穩態造成偏離的合成觀察，以水頭與流量穩定區段說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Permeability flow comparison, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Saturated steady Darcy flow without side leakage; the result is specimen-equivalent permeability. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Trapped air makes initial flow unrepresentative of steady flow. Explain which evidence in stable intervals of head and flow distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「滲透流量比較」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Permeability flow comparison\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用岩石密度會低估運輸與暫存體積","本單元以水頭與流量穩定區段區分模型與觀察，先用穩定水頭時間序列、試體斷面與定時排水量建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Solid-rock density understates transport and storage volume.","Use stable intervals of head and flow to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以水頭與流量穩定區段區分模型與觀察，先用穩定水頭時間序列、試體斷面與定時排水量建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use stable intervals of head and flow to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b344-v16-36","title":"滲透流量比較：失效診斷","titleEn":"Permeability flow comparison: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「滲透流量比較」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Permeability flow comparison” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"空氣滯留會使初期流量不能代表穩態。這個失效與「滲透流量比較」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查水頭與流量穩定區段，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Trapped air makes initial flow unrepresentative of steady flow. This failure and a measurement bias in Permeability flow comparison can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check stable intervals of head and flow rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用水頭與流量穩定區段作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；空氣滯留會使初期流量不能代表穩態，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Trapped air makes initial flow unrepresentative of steady flow; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：空氣滯留會使初期流量不能代表穩態」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Trapped air makes initial flow unrepresentative of steady flow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"空氣滯留會使初期流量不能代表穩態。這個失效與「滲透流量比較」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查水頭與流量穩定區段，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Trapped air makes initial flow unrepresentative of steady flow. This failure and a measurement bias in Permeability flow comparison can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check stable intervals of head and flow rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「滲透流量比較」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Permeability flow comparison\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["空氣滯留會使初期流量不能代表穩態。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把所有差額當成廢料會掩蓋量測問題"],"optionsEn":["Trapped air makes initial flow unrepresentative of steady flow.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Labelling every discrepancy as waste hides measurement faults."],"answer":0,"explanation":"空氣滯留會使初期流量不能代表穩態。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Trapped air makes initial flow unrepresentative of steady flow. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b344-v16-37","title":"未回收物料比例：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Unrecovered material fraction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「未回收物料比例」如何影響道碴清篩與再利用的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Unrecovered material fraction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ballast cleaning and reuse”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"未回收量可以包含秤重誤差、濺散與滯留，不能直接判定偷漏。本模型把 lost 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 3.3 percent。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。分母與差額採同一批次乾質量；比例本身不判定差額原因。使用秤重校正與存量盤點作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把所有差額當成廢料會掩蓋量測問題，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「未回收物料比例」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Unrecovered quantity can include weighing error, spillage and retained inventory; it does not identify a cause by itself. In this model, lost is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 3.3 percent. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Denominator and residual share one batch and dry-mass basis; the ratio does not identify the cause. Use scale calibration and inventory reconciliation as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Labelling every discrepancy as waste hides measurement faults; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Unrecovered material fraction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：lost=3 t, feed=100 t；y=lost/feed*100=3 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: lost=3 t, feed=100 t; y=lost/feed*100=3 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把所有差額當成廢料會掩蓋量測問題」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Labelling every discrepancy as waste hides measurement faults.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「未回收物料比例」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Unrecovered material fraction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-37-k1","title":"未回收物料比例","titleEn":"Unrecovered material fraction","text":"未回收量可以包含秤重誤差、濺散與滯留，不能直接判定偷漏。本模型把 lost 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 3.3 percent。","textEn":"Unrecovered quantity can include weighing error, spillage and retained inventory; it does not identify a cause by itself. In this model, lost is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把所有差額當成廢料會掩蓋量測問題 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Labelling every discrepancy as waste hides measurement faults. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「未回收物料比例」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Unrecovered material fraction\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把所有差額當成廢料會掩蓋量測問題","未回收量可以包含秤重誤差、濺散與滯留，不能直接判定偷漏。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未記錄存料會把正常暫存當成損耗"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Labelling every discrepancy as waste hides measurement faults.","Unrecovered quantity can include weighing error, spillage and retained inventory; it does not identify a cause by itself.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Unrecorded inventory makes temporary storage appear as loss."],"answer":1,"explanation":"未回收量可以包含秤重誤差、濺散與滯留，不能直接判定偷漏。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Unrecovered quantity can include weighing error, spillage and retained inventory; it does not identify a cause by itself. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b344-v16-38","title":"未回收物料比例：定量估算","titleEn":"Unrecovered material fraction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「未回收物料比例」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Unrecovered material fraction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：lost=3 t, feed=100 t；y=lost/feed*100=3 percent。只把 lost 增加百分之十，y=3.3 percent。模型邊界：分母與差額採同一批次乾質量；比例本身不判定差額原因；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: lost=3 t, feed=100 t; y=lost/feed*100=3 percent. Increasing only lost with a ten-percent increase gives y=3.3 percent. Boundary: Denominator and residual share one batch and dry-mass basis; the ratio does not identify the cause; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以秤重校正與存量盤點區分模型與觀察，先用各秤重點校準、容器殘料與物料盤點建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use scale calibration and inventory reconciliation to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：lost=3 t, feed=100 t；y=lost/feed*100=3 percent。只把 lost 增加百分之十，y=3.3 percent。模型邊界：分母與差額採同一批次乾質量；比例本身不判定差額原因；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: lost=3 t, feed=100 t; y=lost/feed*100=3 percent. Increasing only lost with a ten-percent increase gives y=3.3 percent. Boundary: Denominator and residual share one batch and dry-mass basis; the ratio does not identify the cause; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「未回收物料比例」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Unrecovered material fraction\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把全部粗料視為合格會低估新料","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：篩網堵塞會讓細料被錯列為粗料","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：lost=3 t, feed=100 t；y=lost/feed*100=3 percent。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating all coarse material as qualified understates fresh demand.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Screen clogging misclassifies fines as coarse material.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: lost=3 t, feed=100 t; y=lost/feed*100=3 percent."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：lost=3 t, feed=100 t；y=lost/feed*100=3 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: lost=3 t, feed=100 t; y=lost/feed*100=3 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b344-v16-39","title":"未回收物料比例：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Unrecovered material fraction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「未回收物料比例」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Unrecovered material fraction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以秤重校正與存量盤點區分模型與觀察，先用各秤重點校準、容器殘料與物料盤點建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「未回收物料比例」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use scale calibration and inventory reconciliation to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using calibration at each scale, retained container material and inventory count, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Unrecovered material fraction. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「未回收物料比例」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出分母與差額採同一批次乾質量；比例本身不判定差額原因如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把所有差額當成廢料會掩蓋量測問題造成偏離的合成觀察，以秤重校正與存量盤點說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Unrecovered material fraction, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Denominator and residual share one batch and dry-mass basis; the ratio does not identify the cause. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Labelling every discrepancy as waste hides measurement faults. Explain which evidence in scale calibration and inventory reconciliation distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：把所有差額當成廢料會掩蓋量測問題。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Labelling every discrepancy as waste hides measurement faults. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以秤重校正與存量盤點區分模型與觀察，先用各秤重點校準、容器殘料與物料盤點建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「未回收物料比例」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use scale calibration and inventory reconciliation to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using calibration at each scale, retained container material and inventory count, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Unrecovered material fraction. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「未回收物料比例」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出分母與差額採同一批次乾質量；比例本身不判定差額原因如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把所有差額當成廢料會掩蓋量測問題造成偏離的合成觀察，以秤重校正與存量盤點說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Unrecovered material fraction, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Denominator and residual share one batch and dry-mass basis; the ratio does not identify the cause. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Labelling every discrepancy as waste hides measurement faults. Explain which evidence in scale calibration and inventory reconciliation distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「未回收物料比例」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Unrecovered material fraction\"?","options":["本單元以秤重校正與存量盤點區分模型與觀察，先用各秤重點校準、容器殘料與物料盤點建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：短時峰值不代表整班處理量"],"optionsEn":["Use scale calibration and inventory reconciliation to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A short peak rate does not represent shift production."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以秤重校正與存量盤點區分模型與觀察，先用各秤重點校準、容器殘料與物料盤點建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use scale calibration and inventory reconciliation to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b344-v16-40","title":"未回收物料比例：失效診斷","titleEn":"Unrecovered material fraction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b344-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「未回收物料比例」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Unrecovered material fraction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把所有差額當成廢料會掩蓋量測問題。這個失效與「未回收物料比例」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查秤重校正與存量盤點，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Labelling every discrepancy as waste hides measurement faults. This failure and a measurement bias in Unrecovered material fraction can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check scale calibration and inventory reconciliation rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用秤重校正與存量盤點作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把所有差額當成廢料會掩蓋量測問題，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Labelling every discrepancy as waste hides measurement faults; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把所有差額當成廢料會掩蓋量測問題」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Labelling every discrepancy as waste hides measurement faults.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b344-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把所有差額當成廢料會掩蓋量測問題。這個失效與「未回收物料比例」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查秤重校正與存量盤點，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Labelling every discrepancy as waste hides measurement faults. This failure and a measurement bias in Unrecovered material fraction can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check scale calibration and inventory reconciliation rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b344-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「未回收物料比例」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Unrecovered material fraction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把所有差額當成廢料會掩蓋量測問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未記錄存料會把正常暫存當成損耗"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Labelling every discrepancy as waste hides measurement faults.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Unrecorded inventory makes temporary storage appear as loss."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把所有差額當成廢料會掩蓋量測問題。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Labelling every discrepancy as waste hides measurement faults. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-track-clean","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b344-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b344-en.svg"}};
